{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevRatioExpansion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevRatioExpansion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevPeakValue"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_kashaevProd_ratio_gaussian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_kashaevProd_ratio_gaussian","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevRatioExpansion.lean#L230-L336","doc":"**The ratio IS a tilted Gaussian.**  Everything but `2u·log(2 sin θ_k)`\n(the tilt) and `(πu²/N)·cot θ_k` (the Gaussian) is bounded by terms that vanish\non `|u| ≲ √N`.\n\nThis is the statement the Laplace step needs: `g_{k'}/g_k` is\n`e^{tilt + quadratic}` times `1 + o(1)`, with the `o(1)` uniform over the\nwindow.  Compare `KashaevTailBound`, where the corresponding statements are\none-sided and carry different constants on the two sides — those can prove\n`Θ(√N)` and cannot produce `c_σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_cot_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_cot_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevRatioExpansion.lean#L207-L228","doc":"Mean value on `cot`, whose derivative is `−1/sin²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_two_sin_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_two_sin_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevRatioExpansion.lean#L189-L205","doc":"Mean value on `log(2 sin ·)`, whose derivative is `cot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_kashaevProd_ratio_taylor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_kashaevProd_ratio_taylor","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevRatioExpansion.lean#L84-L175","doc":"**The Gaussian appears.**  Taylor-expanding `Λ` about `θ_k` turns the\nmain-term difference into `linear + quadratic`, with the cubic remainder paid\nfor by `M`, any bound on `1/sin²` between the two angles.\n\n`u = k' − k` is a real number, not a natural: `k'` may sit on either side of\n`k`, and the statement is the same in both directions.\n\nThe quadratic coefficient `π·cot θ_k/N` is the `a` of a Gaussian `e^{−a u²}`\nonce `cot θ_k < 0` — which holds throughout `(π/2, π)`, where the saddle\nlives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_kashaevProd_ratio_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_kashaevProd_ratio_le","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevRatioExpansion.lean#L64-L82","doc":"**The ratio, to `O(1/N²)`.**  Nothing but the triangle inequality applied\nto two instances of step 6 — but note what it buys: the bound on the RATIO is\ntwo-sided and uniform, which no tail bound in `KashaevTailBound` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_kashaevProd_sub_main_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_kashaevProd_sub_main_le","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevRatioExpansion.lean#L58-L62","doc":"`log_kashaevProd_asymptotic`, in the named form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.logKashaevMain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.logKashaevMain","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevRatioExpansion.lean#L51-L56","doc":"The main term of `log_kashaevProd_asymptotic`, named. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.logKashaevErr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.logKashaevErr","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevRatioExpansion.lean#L46-L49","doc":"The error bound of `log_kashaevProd_asymptotic`, named. ","signatureChunk":0}]}